---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How accountability works"
  description="A sparse accountable organisation that brings native outcomes to review."
  active="how"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>Accountability<br /><em>without ceremony.</em></h1>
    <p>A sparse organisation gives every outcome one owner, gives production a real worker, and keeps the Exec free for what comes next.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="role-stack" aria-label="Accountability structure">
    <article><span>Exec</span><div><h2>Owns the portfolio.</h2><p>Delegates each executable request to one accountable lead and returns to availability.</p></div></article>
    <article><span>Lead</span><div><h2>Owns one outcome.</h2><p>Frames, observes, redirects and judges. The lead does not quietly become the producer.</p></div></article>
    <article><span>Staff</span><div><h2>Makes the work.</h2><p>One end-to-end worker is the default until a stable seam earns more coordination cost.</p></div></article>
    <article><span>Owner</span><div><h2>Receives the prepared decision.</h2><p>The owner sees a live outcome and the bounded last mile, not internal traffic.</p></div></article>
  </section>

  <section class="layer-explainer">
    <div><h2>Judgement above.<br />Rules at the boundary.<br />Work in the world.</h2></div>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Authority</strong><p>Identity, secrets, budgets, consequential effects and recovery have deterministic boundaries.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Organisation</strong><p>Goals, actors, sparse Work, Attempts, messages and repair stay recoverable and overridable.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Company computer</strong><p>Persistent files, Git, browsers and ordinary tools are where outcomes are made.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="paired-prose native-review-copy">
    <h2>Review the thing itself.</h2>
    <div><p>A live site, playable build, rendered document or executable scenario comes first. Commits, tests and receipts explain the result after it can be opened.</p><p>Before owner judgement, the team materialises the current candidate, live-probes it, links its evidence, asks one exact question and makes the resume condition observable.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
